Update `zcash_lib/sources/equihash.move` to fix hash generation:

Zcash Equihash hash generation formula:
- For n=144, k=5: output_length = (n/(k+1)+1) * (1 << k) / 8 = 600 bytes total
- Each BLAKE2b-256 call produces 32 bytes
- hashes_per_blake = floor(32 * 8 / (n+1)) = floor(256/145) = 1
- hash_length = ceil((n+1)/8) = 19 bytes (not 18)

Correct implementation:
```move
const HASH_LENGTH: u64 = 19;  // ceil(145/8) = 19 bytes
const INDICES_PER_HASH: u64 = 1; // floor(256/145) = 1

fun generate_single_hash(input: &vector<u8>, index: u32, personal: &vector<u8>): vector<u8> {
    // Compute which BLAKE2b block this index falls in
    let block_index = index / INDICES_PER_HASH;
    let offset = (index % INDICES_PER_HASH) * HASH_LENGTH;

    let mut hash_input = *input;
    append_le32(&mut hash_input, block_index);

    let full_hash = blake2b::hash_with_personal(&hash_input, *personal);

    // Extract HASH_LENGTH bytes starting at offset
    extract_bytes(&full_hash, offset, HASH_LENGTH)
}
```

Reference: https://github.com/zcash/zcash/blob/master/src/crypto/equihash.cpp

